/*
Problem: Smallest Integer Divisible by K (LC 1015)
Topic: Math, Modular Arithmetic

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

A repunit is a number consisting only
of digit '1'.

Instead of constructing huge numbers,
keep track of only the remainder.

If the current remainder is r, then
after appending another '1':

newRemainder = (r * 10 + 1) % k

If the remainder ever becomes 0, the
current length is the answer.

If k is divisible by 2 or 5, such a
number can never exist because every
repunit ends with digit 1.

Also, after checking k different
remainders, a remainder must repeat
(Pigeonhole Principle). If no remainder
is 0 by then, the answer is impossible.

--------------------------------------------------

Time: O(k)

Space: O(1)

--------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    int smallestRepunitDivByK(int k) {

        // Impossible cases
        if(k % 2 == 0 || k % 5 == 0)
            return -1;

        int remainder = 0;

        for(int i = 1; i <= k; i++) {

            remainder = (remainder * 10 + 1) % k;

            if(remainder == 0)
                return i;
        }

        return -1;
    }
};
